  "outstanding_asks": [
    {
      "by": "greptile-apps",
      "ask": "Imports break repository guidance: `_polling_engine_app` imports `socketio` inside the helper without needing to avoid a circular dependency.",
      "addressed": true,
      "path": "tests/units/test_app.py",
      "outdated": true
    },
    {
      "by": "greptile-apps",
      "ask": "Callbacks lack required docstrings: `drained_receive` has no docstring, but the repository guide requires Google-style docstrings on all functions.",
      "addressed": true,
      "path": "reflex/app.py",
      "outdated": true
    },
    {
      "by": "FarhanAliRaza",
      "ask": "The drained request still goes to engine.io, and engine.io answers the oversized POST only after `disconnect(sid)` returns. `disconnect()` calls `socket.close(wait=True)`, which blocks in `queue.join()` until a poll GET consumes the CLOSE packet. When no poll is parked at that moment, the POST is never answered. Every later poll for that sid gets `400 'Session is disconnected'` from `_get_socket`, so nothing can consume the packet. The response is held forever.",
      "addressed": true,
      "path": "reflex/app.py",
      "outdated": true
    },
    {
      "by": "FarhanAliRaza",
      "ask": "This assumption does not hold. The engine.io client sends the CONNECT POST and the first poll GET at the same time, so the POST is often rejected before a poll is parked. Without the parked poll, this test hangs in `queue.join()`, which is the defect described on `app.py`. The parked poll hides it.",
      "addressed": true,
      "path": "tests/units/test_app.py",
      "outdated": true
    },
    {
      "by": "cubic-dev-ai",
      "ask": "Strict UTF-8 decoding can abort cleanup for malformed query bytes. Decode the raw query with Latin-1, as the previous implementation did, so oversized requests always reach SID cleanup.",
      "addressed": true,
      "path": "reflex/app.py",
      "outdated": true
    },
    {
      "by": "cubic-dev-ai",
      "ask": "This changelog overstates the fix by guaranteeing an immediate reconnect. The middleware unblocks the failed request and allows reconnection, but the client\u2019s normal reconnect policy still controls when that happens; describe it as allowing or enabling the browser to reconnect instead.",
      "addressed": true,
      "path": "news/+drain-oversized-polling-post.bugfix.md",
      "outdated": true
    },
    {
      "by": "cubic-dev-ai",
      "ask": "This regression test always indexes `eio.sockets` with `\\xff`, not the session ID, because the malformed `x` parameter is appended after `sid`. Extract the SID before appending the parameter, or parse the `sid` query field directly, so the test can reach its intended closure assertion.",
      "addressed": true,
      "path": "tests/units/test_app.py",
      "outdated": false
    },
    {
      "by": "anishgurjar",
      "ask": "Approve the first-time-contributor workflow gate so CI can run on the updated head.",
      "addressed": true
    }
  ],
